From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v0lumehi <aljic.zijad@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 15:07:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] iOS: picture Fit or Fill for screens that are not 16:9

A per-game launcher setting, DM_PICTURE_FIT (fit, the default, or fill).
Fit is today's picture: the largest centered 16:9 rectangle with black bars.
Fill scales the 16:9 picture until it covers the view and crops the overflow,
with no stretching. It applies to the overlay layout (landscape) only. A
portrait or tabletop split keeps the picture fitted in its area above the
controls, where cropping a small picture costs more than the bars.

The touch controls keep the full view. The game's own touch screen is
normalized on the scaled picture, so a touch on the visible part lands
where that part of the picture is (dm_game_touch_point). A TV keeps Fit.

The Duo harness stubs gain front_ios_device_check, which front_ios.m calls
since the device check, so the harness links again.

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#1083
Reason: Players with screens that are not 16:9 can fill the screen, a per-game choice in the iOS shell.
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#545

